# Cost of Parenting

## Stack

Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Stripe, Clerk, Google AdSense.

## Programmatic SEO

- Prioritize performance on `app/cost-of-parenting/[state]/[city]/`.
- Prefer ISR / static params and lean server rendering for city pages.
- Keep auth and interactive forecasting client-side; public baselines stay cacheable.

## Types & data

- Use modular types from `types/parenting.ts`.
- Avoid giant inline arrays in components/pages.
- Keep data fetches and curated datasets in `app/data/` or `lib/`.

## AdSense & monetization

- Reserve fixed space for ad containers to prevent CLS.
- Do not collapse or shift layout when ads load or fail.
- Free-tier surfaces may show ads; Premium flows must not break layout around them.

## Components

- Default to Server Components.
- Add `"use client"` only when hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, etc.) or browser APIs are required.
- Keep interactive calculator/paywall UI modular and separate from SEO page shells.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — client page just for layout
"use client";
export default function CityPage() { return <main>...</main>; }

// ✅ GOOD — server page + client island
export default async function CityPage({ params }) {
  const baseline = getSafeLocationBaseline(...);
  return (
    <main>
      <CostExperienceProvider baseline={baseline}>
        <FamilyCostConsole />
        <CostDataFeed />
      </CostExperienceProvider>
    </main>
  );
}
```
